### **PART B — Dead CLI Options on `i18n translate`**

#### **7. Unused CLI Options on translate Command**

From [tools/i18n-engine/src/cli.ts](tools/i18n-engine/src/cli.ts) lines 156–184:

```typescript
program
  .command("translate")
  .addArgument(new Argument("[space]", "space id, e.g. docs.guides").argOptional())
  .option("--locale <locale>", "one locale")
  .option("--tier <tier>", "every locale in a tier")
  .option("--provider <provider>", "override the default provider profile")
  .option("--concurrency <n>", "override provider concurrency", Number)
  .option("--force", "retranslate even when the cache/PO entry is up to date", false)
  .action((space: string | undefined, opts: { locale?: string }) =>
    withSpace(
      "translate",
      space,
      async (config) => {
        const locales = opts.locale ? [opts.locale] : guidesLocales(config);  // ← ONLY opts.locale used
        for (const locale of locales) {
          // ...
        }
      },
      async (config, spaceId) => {
        const locales = opts.locale ? [opts.locale] : messagesLocales(config, spaceId);  // ← ONLY opts.locale
        // ...
      },
      async (config, spaceId) => {
        const locales = opts.locale ? [opts.locale] : contentLocales(config, spaceId);  // ← ONLY opts.locale
        // ...
      },
    ),
  );
```

**Dead options:**
- `--tier <tier>` — declared but never read from `opts`
- `--provider <provider>` — declared but never read from `opts`
- `--concurrency <n>` — declared but never read from `opts`
- `--force` — declared but never read from `opts`

✅ **Confirmed: all four are dead.**

